NOTE: the ROOT position (before any move) is the position the ENGINE is asked to search.
Its occurrence count in this game is 1 (it is the start). The 8-move line returns to the same
POSITION with the same side to move and castling, but the halfmove clock differs, so whether
the ENGINE's own repetition detector treats the ROOT as drawn is a separate question from
whether python-chess calls the END position a threefold.
